{%- doc -%}
  One card in the row of three the corporate page offers its routes from
  (Figma: 535:22465 — Collection Card 5).

  It renders [ui-collection-card] in its `cta` cut and adds nothing to it, so the
  card here and the cards on a collection page cannot drift apart.

  A block rather than three sets of settings on the section: the file draws three
  and a page that wants a fourth route should be able to add one without a
  developer. Which is also why the media is an image_picker rather than a
  collection — two of the three point at collections and the third at a form, and
  a card that could only be a collection would rule that out.
{%- enddoc -%}

{% render 'ui-collection-card',
  variant: 'cta',
  title: block.settings.title,
  description: block.settings.description,
  image: block.settings.image,
  link: block.settings.link,
  button_label: block.settings.button_label,
  attributes: block.shopify_attributes
%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Card",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:settings.image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "t:settings.heading",
      "default": "Logo Treats"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "description",
      "label": "Description",
      "default": "For branded orders and events."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "link",
      "label": "t:settings.link"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "button_label",
      "label": "Button",
      "default": "Shop now"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Card"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
